      ":question/worked-solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{array}\\right] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c\\left[\\begin{array}{cc|c}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1\\end{array}\\right].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-2y &=0 \\\\ y &=-1,\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=-1$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-2(-1)=0\\,\u21d2\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=-1.$",
